    "evidence_text": " He co-wrote the song \"Back For More\" with Stephen Pearcy on Ratt's album \"Out of the Cellar\".\n\n The song was co-written by Ratt bassist Juan Croucier, guitarist Warren DeMartini, lead singer Stephen Pearcy and songwriter Desmond Child.\n\nStephen Pearcy\n\nStephen Eric Pearcy (born July 3, 1956), known as Stephen Pearcy, is an American musician.\n\n He is best known as the founder, singer, and songwriter of the heavy metal band Ratt.\n\n The song was co-written by famed songwriter Desmond Child, Ratt guitarist Warren DeMartini and lead singer Stephen Pearcy.\n\n\"Wanted Man' is the first track on American heavy metal band Ratt's album \"Out of the Cellar\".\n\n The song was written by Stephen Pearcy, guitarists Robbin Crosby and Warren DeMartini, and album producer Beau Hill.\n\nVicious Delite was an alternative metal band formed by Stephen Pearcy in 1995 after Arcade.\n\n Stephen Pearcy was said to still be in his Ratt form, indeed his voice was just as compelling.\n\n It was written by Ratt vocalist Stephen Pearcy, bassist Juan Croucier, and guitarist Warren DeMartini.",
